  "rationale": "In vivo knockout screen: expanded mouse HSPCs transduced with one of the 10 Bassik mouse sub-libraries (~20,000 elements, 10 guides per gene, non-targeting and safe-targeting controls), transplanted into lethally irradiated recipients (pooled per sub-library), and after 10-12 weeks c-Kit+ Lin- HSPCs and mature lineages (all lineages, B, T, myeloid, erythroid) were sorted. The paper's main comparison (casTLE, Supplementary Data 1) is HSPCs vs all mature lineages; no plasmid or pre-transplant library was deposited, so that is the comparison here. Every guide belongs to one sub-library and each sub-library was transplanted once, so the genome-wide screen has one library per population for every guide; prepare.R splits the combined GEO files into one column per sub-library so that each analysis uses that sub-library's own library sizes (the HSPC/lineage depth ratio ranges from 0.12 for GE to 0.97 for ACOC). The GW_<sub-library> analyses are 1 vs 1 (no residual df: overdispersion pooled over that sub-library's control guides). The gene-expression (GE) sub-library was also screened a second time in an independent transplant (24 recipients, Supplementary Data 2; GSM9339037-42), which gives the one replicated comparison: GE_two_screens uses both GE screens with a screen term, because HSPC and lineage libraries of the same transplant share clones (Spearman 0.33 and 0.54 within a screen versus 0.05-0.26 across), leaving 1 residual df. The coefficient is all lineages vs HSPC, the sign of the casTLE effect: negative means knockouts enriched in HSPCs (the SAGA members Tada2b, Taf5l, Taf6l, Tada1 and Runx1), positive enriched in mature cells. Non-targeting (0None) and safe-targeting (0Safe) guides are the controls. Library composition is extreme (the top 1% of each sub-library's guides hold 82-99% of HSPC reads and 48-81% of lineage reads: oligoclonal engraftment). Median-ratio totals were tried as a sensitivity check but are capped at the largest single count in three HSPC libraries (GE screen, ACOC, U2) and rest on the few guides detected in HSPCs, so library-size totals are kept; neither makes depletion interpretable.",
